---

type: commit type. Common values:
- feat: a new feature
- fix: patches a bug
- docs: documentation-only changes
- refactor: code changes that neither fix a bug nor add a feature
- perf: improves performance
- test: adds or correct tests
- chore: changes to the build process or auxiliary tools

---

scope (optional): Specific affected project area. e.g.,
- mem/vmm
- kernel
- kerr
- arch/x86/cpu

---

short description: Introduction commit description. It should not exceed 50 characters

---

long description: Explanation (why) of changes. Multiple lines can be used.
It's not recommended to exceed 70 characters per line.

